{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BlockwiseExclusion"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.door_needs_one_of_two_mechanisms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.door_needs_one_of_two_mechanisms","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L220-L233","doc":"**A submodular total needs a block realising one of the two mechanisms.**  This is the\nmixed-sign replacement for `reweight_cannot_open_door`: dropping the `0 ≤ w` hypothesis, one\ncannot conclude supermodularity, but one *can* still name where the door must come from.\n\nRetained as the general statement, but note it is **not** the operative one under convention D,\nwhere `0 ≤ w` holds and `reweight_cannot_open_door` applies directly.  It\nstrictly refines `Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.submodular_needs_interfering_block`, which only asserts\nthe existence of a block with negative contribution — here that block is classified. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.door_mechanism_dichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.door_mechanism_dichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L197-L218","doc":"**Exhaustive dichotomy of the two door mechanisms.**  A block can only push the total\nsubmodular in one of exactly two structurally distinct ways:\n\n* `0 < w ∧ d < 0` — **submodular geometry carried by a positive weight**: a genuine\n  Fréchet–Hoeffding violation (the block's joint damping falls below `r_a + r_b − 1`);\n* `w < 0 ∧ 0 < d` — **supermodular geometry carried by a negative weight**: no Fréchet\n  violation at all, just a sign-indefinite Wedderburn coefficient.\n\nConflating these reports a bookkeeping sign as a geometric fact.  They are measured\nseparately by `mu3_frechet_perblock_probe.py`.\n\n**Under convention D the second branch is VACUOUS.**  `w < 0` never occurs on the physical\nspectrum (see `reweight_cannot_open_door` above: zero negative `y_λ` for `n = 4 … 12`), so a\nsubmodular total can only come from the first mechanism — submodular geometry carried by a\npositive weight.  The dichotomy itself is a theorem about arbitrary reals and is unaffected;\nwhat changes is which branch the physics can occupy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.secondDiff_eq_baseline_mul_slack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.secondDiff_eq_baseline_mul_slack","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L188-L195","doc":"**The Fréchet slack IS the normalized second difference.**  In damping coordinates\n`Δ² = c·(r_ab − (r_a + r_b − 1))`, i.e. the baseline times the Fréchet–Hoeffding slack.  This\nis what makes the slack the weight-independent invariant: the block weight `y_λ` cancels out of\nevery ratio `r`, so the slack is a statement about the *character* alone, and the weight enters\nonly as the outer factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.reweight_cannot_open_door","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.reweight_cannot_open_door","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L155-L184","doc":"**Re-weighting cannot rescue a Fréchet-obeying spectrum.**  If every block's own second\ndifference is non-negative (each block Fréchet-obeying, per\n`Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.frechet_lower_bound_supermodular`), then *any* non-negative\nre-weighting `w_λ ≥ 0` of the blocks is still supermodular.\n\n**The hypothesis `0 ≤ w` is the whole content, and under the production convention it HOLDS —\nso this lemma DOES foreclose the escape \"keep the operator, change the Wedderburn weights\".**\n\nUnder convention D, `y_λ = [n−2k+1]_q / [2]_q^n ≥ 0` on the two-row stratum `λ = (n−k, k)` and\n`y_λ = 0` identically for `ℓ(λ) ≥ 3` (`QOU.QBeta.TemperleyLiebTower`, sorry-free).  Measured over\n`n = 4 … 12` at `q₀`: **zero negative weights at every n** — the blocks split into a positive\ntwo-row stratum and a vanishing `ℓ(λ) ≥ 3` radical.  So `0 ≤ w` is satisfied on the physical\nspectrum and the sum is supermodular.\n\n**Superseded C-frame claim, kept for readers of the older audits.**  This docstring previously\nread *\"the hypothesis FAILS on the physical spectrum … at `n = 9, q₀`, 10 of the 30 weights are\nnegative\"*, citing `docs/audits/2026-05-19-weight-factor-audit.md` §W3 and\n`computations/deltalambda/mu3-frechet-perblock.witness.json`.  Both belong to the **excised\nconvention C**, where `y_λ` was genuinely sign-indefinite for `n ≥ 4`.  The content block\n`mass-theory/y-lambda-sign-pattern` withdrew that claim on 2026-08-09; this file did not follow\nuntil the cited witness was itself drained of convention C.  Two further cautions about the old\nfigure: \"10 of 30\" was a hardcoded literal in the probe, never computed, and it did not match\nthat witness's own payload (20 of 60).\n\nConsequence for the door: the mixed-sign machinery below is not reached under D.  See\n`door_mechanism_dichotomy`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.mu3_slot_ne_blockwise_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.mu3_slot_ne_blockwise_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L134-L151","doc":"**`μ₃ > 0` is unreachable under the corrected slot assembly**, for any per-block\nmultiplicatively-damped trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.slot_nonneg_blockwise_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.slot_nonneg_blockwise_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L113-L132","doc":"**The exclusion survives the slot correction, blockwise.**  If every Wedderburn block is\nmultiplicatively damped by the three bonds (factors in `[0,1]`, non-negative bases), the\ncorrected slot `∑_{pairs}Δ²g + Δ³g` is non-negative — so a **positive** `μ₃` cannot equal it.\n\nTogether with `Mu3BlockwiseExclusion.mu3_ne_blockwise_multiplicative_cluster` this closes the\nper-block multiplicative class against **both** the raw pair reading and the GAP-7-corrected\nslot reading of the μ₃ residual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.slot_nonneg_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.slot_nonneg_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L86-L111","doc":"**The slot sum of a single multiplicative block is non-negative.**\n`∑_{pairs}Δ² + Δ³ = c(uv + uw + vw − uvw)` with `u = 1−r_a`, `v = 1−r_b`, `w = 1−r_c`.\nFactoring as `uv(1−w) + uw + vw` shows it is `≥ 0`: the triple term never outweighs the three\npair terms.\n\n**Sharp hypotheses.**  This needs `u, v, w ≥ 0` (i.e. all three `r ≤ 1`, each bond damps) but\nonly the *single* extra bound `w ≤ 1` (i.e. `0 ≤ r_c`), which is what makes `uv(1−w) ≥ 0`.\nThe lower bounds on `r_a, r_b` are **not** needed — the factoring singles out one bond, and by\nsymmetry it suffices that *some* one of the three has `r ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.thirdDiff_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.thirdDiff_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L75-L82","doc":"**The third difference of a multiplicative block flips sign.**\n`Δ³ = −c(1−r_a)(1−r_b)(1−r_c)`, non-positive for damping factors `≤ 1` — the opposite sign\nto `Δ² = +c(1−r_a)(1−r_b)`.  So the triple term pushes *toward* the μ₃ door. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.thirdDiff_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.thirdDiff_sum","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**`Δ³` commutes with finite sums** — the three-bond analogue of `secondDiff_sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.thirdDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3SlotExclusion.thirdDiff","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3SlotExclusion.lean#L59-L62","doc":"The **third mixed finite difference** on the three-bond Boolean lattice:\n`Δ³g = g_abc − g_ab − g_ac − g_bc + g_a + g_b + g_c − g_∅`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}